{"title":"Mock Geometry AIME 2011 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_Geometry_AIME_2011_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a unit square, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae95e22ca7c2ba5a11b78ea60d7dade798a0783c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB_1C_1D_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> be its image after a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degree rotation about point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8207b79435a4bd499da7598fb44424c8a8499238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> The area of the region consisting of all points inside at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae95e22ca7c2ba5a11b78ea60d7dade798a0783c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB_1C_1D_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb41f89d747dc53308bd681376da9a50173460b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a-\\sqrt{b}} {c},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> shares no perfect square common factor with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f83de90288e19082ad3e20ae97127495aba51430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_Geometry_AIME_2011_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7667c22ac87b65db6de7bf0a2965dcaf3772d9ac.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(5cm); draw(unitsquare); draw((0,1)--(1/2, (2-sqrt(3))/2)--((1+sqrt(3))/2,(3-sqrt(3))/2)--(sqrt(3)/2,3/2)--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(0,1),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(1,1),E); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(1,0),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$B_1$&quot;,(sqrt(3)/2,3/2),N); label(&quot;$C_1$&quot;,((1+sqrt(3))/2,(3-sqrt(3))/2),ENE); label(&quot;$D_1$&quot;,(1/2,(2-sqrt(3))/2),SSW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(1,(3-sqrt(3))/3),SE); draw((0,1)--(1,(3-sqrt(3))/3)); [/asy]\" width=\"378\" height=\"402\" />\n</p><p>Denote the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0dbb274e173a5300efde04a08c92f4fb88ffa96b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1D_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Also, denote a polygon enclosed in square brackets as the area as that polygon. (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd3361fb9586094387d885d23e9efce948e8b291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the area of polygon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.)\n</p><p>The area of the union of the two squares is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38b3db6c7a5c67d5f1cb03d66b22d06875da337.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD]+[AB_1C_1D_1]-[ABED_1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b6266b2a1d2018141058d47847a325c08c2b081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABCD]=[AB_1C_1D_1]=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />, so we wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef20c4c546c7310a536c8383cca8018c0bb2771f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-[ABED_1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Draw in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37dc78eb38542a829693f09a31caeb08eaa02c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED_1\\cong\\triangle AEB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540880d8540f40f1d1f96179ba7b296f68779064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABE=\\angle AD_1E=90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/9/2a91c9f07f503d5f584b397d1489f89af892e776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD_1=AB=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/c/4dca8c840b5e7990251f66b0f94cb1807d11b8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=AE$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, so the triangles are congruent by HL. Thus, their areas are equal, and we need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c4de9956cac01477c897f24f2278de5aec7121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-2[ABE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/036bab0a77f3bf39127b562d428df43aeacdb648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAB_1=30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, since that's the angle of rotation, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9208a5a74468352f77c278ef39e73a6c43070588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D_1AB=90^\\circ-30^\\circ=60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/90549d32b4c9cebe12664493ad0fdce845766828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D_1AE=\\angle EAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"142\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486a14da2221eb3d57186bbfda8febced61389b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAB=\\frac{60^\\circ}{2}=30^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Now we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73cf4df1bdc304490d5a6fd12bd3878c35b1140f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=BA\\cdot\\tan\\angle EAB=1\\cdot\\tan30^\\circ=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"332\" height=\"41\" />. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b554eef62ce43ea49b8d2cfbb496c33b39821433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABE]=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot1\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"204\" height=\"41\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/9/87956ad2f3935dbc30ffabfea058122f76d5c093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-2\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\right)=\\frac{6-\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"182\" height=\"53\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4ad237d7950b33d0cb017de429a7fe0ea174fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=\\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_Geometry_AIME_2011_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=OEkt8HbUVbQ\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=OEkt8HbUVbQ</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040929\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 178/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6772/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10580:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040929 and revision id 184557. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}